# PERMANENT STRICT PROJECT RULE - DATA INTEGRITY MANDATE

Under NO circumstances should any test, script, or operation delete, drop, reset, truncate, or overwrite existing records, documents, or collections in MongoDB Atlas or Redis.

1. Tests MUST be unit-scoped with in-memory or mocked databases, or use safe read-only operations.
2. Production data (Tenants, Menus, Products, Categories, Orders, Users) is SACROSANCT and must remain 100% intact.
3. Never run destructive integration cleanup commands against the shared cluster.
